      {
        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on scope, key pain points, and confirm the quarter-end close workflow map.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 440036,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, kicking off the Quarter-End Financial Close Process Streamlining project. The main goal is to standardize and speed up our close. To start on T1, let's map the current process. What are the biggest pain points or bottlenecks you face each quarter? All input is welcome.",
            "mentions": [
              5553,
              75794,
              98074,
              326471
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 5553,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "For me, it's the manual reconciliation of accruals. We spend a lot of time chasing down supporting documents from different departments right before the deadline.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "raised_hands",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 75794,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "I agree, there are communication issues. Sometimes I'm not sure which version of a spreadsheet is the final one.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 98074,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "The way we post journal entries is not very consistent. Different people use different descriptions which makes the review process harder.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 440036,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Thanks, all. These are great points. Document chasing, version control, and inconsistent JEs. Let's make sure the new workflow in A1 addresses these specifically.",
            "mentions": [
              5553,
              75794,
              98074
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 326471,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "One more critical point: the inter-company transaction reconciliation. It's a major dependency for almost everything else, but it's not formally tracked as a distinct step. This causes a cascade of delays if it's not completed on day one. We should map it as a priority task.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 440036,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "Excellent point, that's a huge one. I've added it to the list. So, for the initial map for T1, I've listed these activities: \n1. Inter-company reconciliations\n2. Accrual & provision calculations\n3. Fixed asset depreciation runs\n4. Bank & cash reconciliation\n5. Revenue recognition checks\n6. Final trial balance review\nDoes this list seem complete for now? We can refine it in A1.",
            "mentions": [
              326471
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1",
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 75794,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "What about checking invoices?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 5553,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "I think that's part of the accrual and revenue checks, right?",
            "mentions": [
              75794
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 440036,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "Exactly, let's keep it at this level for the main workflow. We can detail sub-tasks later. If everyone is okay with this list, we can lock it in.",
            "mentions": [
              5553
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 440036,
            "reply_to": "M10",
            "text": "Great, that's a decision then. For mapping the 'as-is' process and for our later simulation, we need a reference period. I propose we use last quarter's close (Q2). It had enough complexity to be a good test case. Any objections?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M12",
            "speaker_id": 326471,
            "reply_to": "M11",
            "text": "Q2 is a good choice. It included that large one-time asset disposal, which will be a solid test for our exception handling process.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M13",
            "speaker_id": 98074,
            "reply_to": "M11",
            "text": "Q2 works for me.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M14",
            "speaker_id": 440036,
            "reply_to": "M13",
            "text": "Perfect. We'll use Q2 as our reference. That's our second decision. I'll start drafting the workflow in A1 based on this and will share it for review by EOD tomorrow.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
